Z||000000||Pheagey||10-08-2001||10:03 AM||||I got new front tires recent and is smoothut out my driving dramaticly (I can now do 80+ with no problem). But now I notice a slight vibration throught my pedal. It is not constant, the vibiration comes in a rythm, very perdictable. Any suggections? Alos fi it help when I press the gas pedal new 3/4 to the floor it has a slight clunck to it. When I let off the pedal it cluncks at the same place.<BR>Thanks in advance. <A HREF="Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html" TARGET=_blank>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Pheagey Grean<BR>"There my hero's, every one of them..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||10-08-2001||10:08 AM||||Sounds like 2 issues, first your throttle cable sounds like it's a bit worn, OR the linkage at the back needs some greese, spray the hell out of the throttle linkage on the Throttle body with penetrating oil then coat with a grease of some sort.<P>As for the vibration, I have the same thing, it's caused by un matched tires, you have different tires on the front and back.  I have the same thing, I am getting new matched tires in the spring.||||reg||1
